# ─── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in both values, then restart `npm run dev`.
#
# Where to get them:
#   1. Open your project at https://supabase.com/dashboard
#   2. Project Settings → API Keys  (older dashboards: Settings → API)
#   3. URL              → "Project URL"          e.g. https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
#      Publishable key  → "Publishable key" (starts `sb_publishable_...`)
#                         or, on older projects, the "anon / public" key (a JWT
#                         starting `eyJ...`). Either works — see note below.
#
# Both of these are safe to expose in the browser: they are public keys and every
# table is protected by Row Level Security (see supabase/schema.sql).
#
# Do NOT put the service_role / secret key in this app. It bypasses RLS and is
# not needed — privileged work happens inside the submit_judgment SQL function.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# If your project only offers the older key name, use this line instead of the
# one above — the app accepts either and prefers PUBLISHABLE_KEY when both are set.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...


# ─── Database (optional, tooling only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed to apply schema.sql / seed.sql from the command line with psql.
# The running app never reads this — it talks to Supabase over HTTP with the
# publishable key above. Leave it blank if you use the dashboard SQL editor.
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI,
# then replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password. Use the session
# pooler on port 5432, not the transaction pooler on 6543 — schema.sql uses
# DO $$ blocks and function definitions that need a real session.
#
# ⚠ This credential bypasses Row Level Security entirely. Never ship it to the
# browser, never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, and rotate it if it leaks.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.your-project-ref:PASSWORD@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres


# ─── After filling these in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Apply the schema, either way:
#      dashboard → SQL Editor → paste supabase/schema.sql, then supabase/seed.sql
#      or: psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/schema.sql -f supabase/seed.sql
# 2. Authentication → Sign In / Providers → turn OFF "Confirm email".
#    The login page uses email + password; the built-in mailer caps at ~2
#    messages/hour, which is why magic link is commented out in login/page.tsx.
# 3. If you re-enable magic link, add these under Authentication → URL
#    Configuration → Redirect URLs:
#      http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#      https://<your-production-domain>/auth/callback
# 4. npm run dev
